1	---
2	component: component.text-area
3	package: "@taproot-ds/web-components"
4	tagName: ds-text-area
5	defineExport: defineTextArea
6	usage: |
7	  <ds-text-area label="Project description" name="description" rows="4" required></ds-text-area>
8	api:
9	  - { name: label, kind: attribute, parameter: label }
10	  - { name: hint, kind: attribute, parameter: hint }
11	  - { name: error, kind: attribute, parameter: error }
12	  - { name: name, kind: attribute, parameter: name }
13	  - { name: value, kind: attribute, parameter: value }
14	  - { name: disabled, kind: attribute, parameter: disabled }
15	  - { name: required, kind: attribute, parameter: required }
16	  - { name: placeholder, kind: attribute, parameter: placeholder }
17	  - { name: autocomplete, kind: attribute, parameter: autocomplete }
18	  - { name: rows, kind: attribute, parameter: rows }
19	  - { name: readonly, kind: attribute, parameter: readonly }
20	  - { name: value, kind: property, parameter: value }
21	  - name: form
22	    kind: property
23	    type: "HTMLFormElement | null"
24	    description: The associated form, including association across the shadow boundary.
25	  - { name: input, kind: event, event: input }
26	  - { name: change, kind: event, event: change }
27	---
28	
29	## Forms
30	
31	Set `name` to include the current value in form submission. The `value` attribute supplies the
32	initial value; the `value` property changes the current value without changing the reset value.
33	A non-empty `error` blocks submission.
34	
35	To validate in your own code, set `novalidate` on the form so the submit reaches your listener.
36	Read the values there, and set `error` on each field that needs a correction. Clear `error` on the
37	field's `input` event and when the form resets, because a reset leaves it set.
38	
39	`rows` accepts positive whole numbers and defaults to four. `readonly` preserves focus and submission while preventing edits. Users can resize the control vertically.
